window.CLIPS=Object.assign(window.CLIPS||{},{"Ribosome. Memory hook: Factory robot. Builds proteins from amino acids. Not membrane-bound. Thousands per cell, on the ER or floating. Found in ALL cells. If it's missing: No proteins get made, so the cell can't repair or grow.":"","Endoplasmic Reticulum (ER). Memory hook: Train: All aboard!. Tubes and sacs that transport proteins inside the cell. Rough ER has ribosomes; smooth ER has none. If it's missing: Proteins get stuck where they were made.":"","Adaptation & Evolution. An adaptation is an inherited trait that helps survival. Evolution means populations change over many generations as helpful traits get passed on. Individuals do NOT choose their traits.":"","Chloroplast. Memory hook: Sugar jar. Plants only. Green chlorophyll uses sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to make sugar by photosynthesis. If it's missing: The plant can't make food and starves.":"","Trash can / garbage disposal , Breaks down waste, worn-out parts, and invading bacteria and viruses. Mainly in animal cells; plants use a lytic vacuole.":"","Water tank: Let's go in for a dip! , Stores water, food, and waste. Plants have one LARGE vacuole that keeps their shape; animals have many small ones.":"","Factory robot , Builds proteins from amino acids. Not membrane-bound. Thousands per cell, on the ER or floating. Found in ALL cells.":"","Organelles Work Together. Ribosomes make proteins, the ER moves them, and the Golgi packages and ships them. Mitochondria power it all.":"","Oops! It's FALSE. Fix: Homeostasis means maintaining stable internal conditions. (Change over generations is evolution.)":"","UPS truck , 5 to 8 stacked sacs. Modifies, sorts, and packages proteins and lipids and ships them out.":"","Individuals don't choose traits; populations change over generations as inherited traits affect survival.":"","Homeostasis. Keeping stable internal conditions, like sweating to cool down or shivering to warm up.":"","Oops! It's FALSE. Fix: MITOCHONDRIA release energy; chloroplasts make sugar from light.":"","True or false: Individual organisms choose to change their traits to survive.":"","The blank is the jelly-like material inside the cell where organelles are found.":"","Test finished. You scored 17 out of 25, 68 percent.":"","Test finished. You scored 21 out of 25, 84 percent.":"","Test finished. You scored 16 out of 25, 64 percent.":"","Not quite. The answer is Organ , then cell , then tissue , then organism":"","Test finished. You scored 11 out of 25, 44 percent.":"","Not quite. The answer is Maintaining stable internal conditions":"","Cell , then tissue , then organ , then organ system , then organism":"","Test finished. You scored 15 out of 25, 60 percent.":"","Resource availability affects survival and population size":"","Individual organisms choose to change their traits to survive.":"","The answer is Cell , then organ , then tissue , then organism.":"","Test finished. You scored 2 out of 25, 8 percent.":"","Not quite. The answer is Only animals are made of cells":"","Quiz over! You got 6 out of 10. Great job Richard!":"","Not quite. The answer is Mitochondria and lysosomes":"","Sorry, I didn't catch that. Try again or tap your answer.":"","Homeostasis means changing over many generations.":"","Not quite. The answer is All organisms survive":"","True or false: Bacteria are eukaryotic cells.":"","Which is an example of a prokaryotic organism?":"","The blank modify, sort, and package materials.":"","The answer is Jelly-like fluid holding organelles.":"","The blank controls what enters and leaves the cell.":"","Tissue , then cell , then organ , then organism":"","The answer is All living things are made of cells.":"","The answer is Only animals are made of cells.":"","A blank breaks down waste and worn-out parts.":"","Organs work together to form organ systems.":"","The blank transports materials within the cell.":"","Modifies, sorts, packages materials":"","The blank uses light energy to make sugar.":"","Not quite. The answer is Mitochondrion":"","The answer is Stores water and materials.":"","Not quite. The answer is Cytoplasm":"","Not quite. The answer is Bacterium":"","Not quite. The answer is Vacuole":"","Endoplasmic Reticulum (ER)":"","Not quite. The answer is Mushroom":"","The answer is Only plants compete.":"","Jelly-like fluid holding organelles":"","The answer is Mitochondrion.":"","Only animals are made of cells":"","The answer is mitochondria.":"","You got 19 out of 22":"","You matched 11 out of 11":"","You got 11 out of 22":"","The answer is Golgi bodies.":"","You got 0 out of 22":"","The answer is Golgi body.":"","Releases energy from food":"","Plant cells have a cell wall.":"","You matched 7 out of 11":"","You matched 9 out of 11":"","Cell wall and chloroplasts":"","The answer is Ribosome.":"","You got 3 out of 22":"","You matched 1 out of 11":"","The answer is adaptation.":"","Endoplasmic reticulum":"","The answer is cytoplasm.":"","A blank builds proteins.":"","You matched 2 out of 11":"","The answer is Bacterium.":"","The answer is Vacuole.":"","The answer is Oak tree.":"","The answer is cell wall.":"","Transports materials in the cell":"","Correct! It's TRUE.":"","The answer is False.":"","Breaking down waste":"","Number 17.":"","homeostasis":"","Mitochondria":"","Oops! It's TRUE.":"","True or false?":"","Golgi body":"","Number 7.":"","Number 20.":"","adaptation":"","lysosome":"","ribosome":"","Number 6.":"","Number 10.":"","Cell Wall":"","cell wall":"","Correct!":"","evolution":"","tissue":"","A":""});